recommend check-in (Claude) TABLECLOTH'S FOUR BOUNDS ALL STAND ON DESKS NOW, and the fourth is the one that needed a shape the room did not have: a number with an alphabet standing beside it. `max_name = 48` bounds a name's LENGTH, and the manifest grammar needs that a name carry neither of the two bytes its line is split on -- two facts, neither following from the other, which is REDS %354 read one layer up. So the desk shows the number and lists the bytes, and three readings carry it that can each fail while the other two agree: the number equals `max_name`, the listed bytes equal what `name_is_one_field` actually refuses, and `store_artifact` still consults that wall. That third reading is the one worth arguing for -- a function refusing exactly the right bytes refuses nothing at all while no caller asks it, and without it a desk can display an invariant the module stopped honoring. Proven from both sides: the control runs forty-one cases in a throwaway pen, 6 welcomes and 35 refusals and 0 wrong, and its case 35 is the whole point -- a third byte joins the wall in the Rye alone, 48 still equals 48 on both sides, and a length-only guard would have stayed perfectly quiet. All four desks lower through Glow and run to EXIT:0. I ALSO OWN A RED FROM MY OWN LAST LAP AND CHOSE NOT TO BOOK IT. This witness's header claimed the guard carries no roster of its own, which is true of the scan and false of the witness, whose asserts pin the nine ClothError names -- so an honest tenth path reds a file that promised it would not. I measured before deciding: one file of twenty-six Tend witnesses does this, so it is an instance rather than a family and there is no loom owed. The pin has a real job the comparison cannot do, since two rooms compared against each other can never see all three changing together -- so the sentence moved rather than the assert, and the header now names both pinned lists and what an honest change costs. Cutting to the depth the truth requires, which is the fire row's own lesson. TWO THINGS ABOVE MY HAND. `pond/apps/spool_cloth.rye` carries the identical bound and the identical wall with no pedestal, and my byte reader would read it unchanged -- Hush's file, so it is on the card rather than in this commit. And the card itself opened at 24,555 of 24,576 and closed at 24,565; that is two laps running where a living pin's bound has priced the round, and %347 says widening it is yours.
